        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/a8a7844f/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator/design.md",
        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-02-03\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis design specifies a command-line YAML validator for the rp1-eval-project. The validator accepts a file path, parses the YAML content using a custom parser (to satisfy the no-dependencies constraint), and reports validity with appropriate exit codes.\n\n**Key Design Decisions:**\n- Custom YAML parser implementation (Bun lacks built-in YAML support)\n- Full parse-to-object approach for thorough validation\n- Follows existing codebase patterns (TypeScript, src/ structure, bun:test)\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    CLI[validate.ts<br/>CLI Entry Point] --> Parser[yaml-parser.ts<br/>YAML Parser]\n    CLI --> FS[Bun File API]\n    CLI --> Output[Console Output]\n    CLI --> Exit[Process Exit Code]\n\n    Parser --> Lexer[Lexer<br/>Tokenization]\n    Parser --> AST[Parser<br/>Object Construction]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### 2.1 Component Architecture\n\nThe implementation consists of three main components:\n\n| Component | File | Responsibility |\n|-----------|------|----------------|\n| CLI Entry Point | `src/validate.ts` | Argument parsing, file reading, output formatting, exit codes |\n| YAML Parser | `src/yaml-parser.ts` | Tokenization and parsing of YAML to JavaScript objects |\n| Package Config | `package.json` | Script registration for `bun run validate` |\n\n### 2.2 Component Interaction\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as validate.ts\n    participant FS as Bun.file()\n    participant Parser as yaml-parser.ts\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate config.yaml\n    CLI->>CLI: Parse arguments\n    alt No file path provided\n        CLI->>User: Usage instructions\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n    CLI->>FS: Read file\n    alt File not found\n        CLI->>User: \"Error: File not found\"\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n    FS-->>CLI: File content\n    CLI->>Parser: parseYaml(content)\n    alt Parse success\n        Parser-->>CLI: Parsed object\n        CLI->>User: \"Valid YAML: config.yaml\"\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(0)\n    else Parse failure\n        Parser-->>CLI: YamlParseError\n        CLI->>User: \"Invalid YAML: config.yaml\\n[error details]\"\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 YAML Parser Module\n\n**File**: `src/yaml-parser.ts`\n\nThe parser implements a two-phase approach: lexical analysis (tokenization) followed by recursive descent parsing.\n\n#### 3.1.1 Supported YAML Constructs\n\n| Construct | Example | Support Level |\n|-----------|---------|---------------|\n| Key-value pairs | `key: value` | Full |\n| Nested objects | Indentation-based | Full |\n| Arrays (block) | `- item` | Full |\n| Arrays (inline) | `[a, b, c]` | Full |\n| Objects (inline) | `{a: 1, b: 2}` | Full |\n| Strings (plain) | `hello world` | Full |\n| Strings (quoted) | `\"hello\"`, `'world'` | Full |\n| Strings (multiline) | `\\|`, `>` | Full |\n| Numbers | `42`, `3.14`, `-7` | Full |\n| Booleans | `true`, `false`, `yes`, `no` | Full |\n| Null | `null`, `~`, empty | Full |\n| Comments | `# comment` | Full (ignored) |\n| Anchors/Aliases | `&anchor`, `*alias` | Not supported |\n| Custom tags | `!tag` | Not supported |\n\n#### 3.1.2 Parser Interface\n\n```typescript\n// Public API\nexport function parseYaml(content: string): unknown;\n\n// Error class\nexport class YamlParseError extends Error {\n  constructor(\n    message: string,\n    public readonly line: number,\n    public readonly column: number\n  ) {\n    super(`${message} at line ${line}, column ${column}`);\n    this.name = 'YamlParseError';\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### 3.1.3 Internal Structure\n\n```typescript\n// Token types for lexer\ntype TokenType =\n  | 'KEY'           // identifier followed by colon\n  | 'VALUE'         // scalar value\n  | 'INDENT'        // indentation increase\n  | 'DEDENT'        // indentation decrease\n  | 'NEWLINE'       // line break\n  | 'DASH'          // array item marker\n  | 'COLON'         // key-value separator\n  | 'LBRACKET'      // inline array start\n  | 'RBRACKET'      // inline array end\n  | 'LBRACE'        // inline object start\n  | 'RBRACE'        // inline object end\n  | 'COMMA'         // inline separator\n  | 'PIPE'          // literal block scalar\n  | 'GREATER'       // folded block scalar\n  | 'EOF';          // end of file\n\ninterface Token {\n  type: TokenType;\n  value: string;\n  line: number;\n  column: number;\n}\n\n// Internal parser class\nclass YamlLexer {\n  tokenize(content: string): Token[];\n}\n\nclass YamlParser {\n  parse(tokens: Token[]): unknown;\n}\n```\n\n#### 3.1.4 Parsing Algorithm\n\n1. **Lexer Phase**: Convert input string to token stream\n   - Track indentation levels using a stack\n   - Emit INDENT/DEDENT tokens for nesting changes\n   - Handle quoted strings with escape sequences\n   - Skip comments\n\n2. **Parser Phase**: Build JavaScript object from tokens\n   - Recursive descent parser\n   - Use indentation tokens to determine structure\n   - Convert scalar values to appropriate JS types\n\n### 3.2 CLI Entry Point\n\n**File**: `src/validate.ts`\n\n```typescript\n// Main entry point\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  const filePath = process.argv[2];\n\n  // Validate arguments\n  if (!filePath) {\n    printUsage();\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  // Read and validate file\n  try {\n    const content = await readFile(filePath);\n    parseYaml(content);\n    console.log(`Valid YAML: ${filePath}`);\n    process.exit(0);\n  } catch (error) {\n    handleError(error, filePath);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n\n// Helper functions\nfunction printUsage(): void;\nfunction readFile(filePath: string): Promise<string>;\nfunction handleError(error: unknown, filePath: string): void;\n```\n\n#### 3.2.1 Output Messages\n\n| Scenario | Output Format |\n|----------|---------------|\n| Success | `Valid YAML: {filepath}` |\n| Invalid YAML | `Invalid YAML: {filepath}`<br/>`Error: {message}` |\n| File not found | `Error: File not found: {filepath}` |\n| Read error | `Error: Cannot read file: {filepath}`<br/>`{error message}` |\n| No arguments | `Usage: bun run validate <file.yaml>`<br/>`Validates YAML file syntax.` |\n\n#### 3.2.2 Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Condition |\n|------|-----------|\n| 0 | File exists and contains valid YAML |\n| 1 | Any error (invalid YAML, file not found, read error, missing args) |\n\n### 3.3 Data Model\n\n```mermaid\nerDiagram\n    YamlDocument ||--o{ YamlValue : contains\n    YamlValue ||--o| YamlObject : \"can be\"\n    YamlValue ||--o| YamlArray : \"can be\"\n    YamlValue ||--o| YamlScalar : \"can be\"\n    YamlObject ||--o{ YamlValue : \"has values\"\n    YamlArray ||--o{ YamlValue : \"has items\"\n\n    YamlScalar {\n        string stringValue\n        number numberValue\n        boolean booleanValue\n        null nullValue\n    }\n```\n\nThe parser outputs standard JavaScript types:\n- Objects: `Record<string, unknown>`\n- Arrays: `unknown[]`\n- Scalars: `string | number | boolean | null`\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Rationale |\n|-------|------------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Project standard; required per dependencies |\n| Language | TypeScript | Project standard; strict mode enabled |\n| File I/O | Bun.file() | Built-in, no dependencies required |\n| Testing | bun:test | Project standard; existing pattern |\n| YAML Parsing | Custom implementation | REQ-008 prohibits external dependencies |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Estimated Complexity |\n|---|-----------|-------------|---------------------|\n| T1 | YAML Parser | Implement lexer and parser in `src/yaml-parser.ts` | High |\n| T2 | CLI Entry Point | Implement `src/validate.ts` with argument handling and output | Low |\n| T3 | Package Script | Add `validate` script to `package.json` | Trivial |\n| T4 | Unit Tests | Create `src/yaml-parser.test.ts` and `src/validate.test.ts` | Medium |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T3] - Parser module and package.json script have no code dependencies\n2. [T2] - CLI entry point requires parser module\n3. [T4] - Tests require both parser and CLI modules\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (interface dependency: CLI imports parseYaml from parser)\n- T4 -> [T1, T2] (test dependency: tests import modules under test)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    T1[T1: YAML Parser] --> T2[T2: CLI Entry Point]\n    T3[T3: Package Script]\n    T1 --> T4[T4: Unit Tests]\n    T2 --> T4\n\n    style T1 fill:#f9f,stroke:#333\n    style T3 fill:#9f9,stroke:#333\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### 7.1 Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Category | Value | Include |\n|---------------|-------|---------|\n| Parser correctness (valid YAML) | HIGH - core business logic | Yes |\n| Parser error detection (invalid YAML) | HIGH - core business logic | Yes |\n| CLI argument handling | MEDIUM - app-specific behavior | Yes |\n| CLI exit codes | HIGH - CI/CD integration contract | Yes |\n| File reading errors | MEDIUM - error handling paths | Yes |\n| Bun.file() behavior | LOW - testing framework | No |\n\n### 7.2 Test Plan\n\n**File**: `src/yaml-parser.test.ts`\n\n| Test Case | Input | Expected |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Parse empty document | `` | `null` |\n| Parse simple key-value | `key: value` | `{key: \"value\"}` |\n| Parse nested object | `a:\\n  b: c` | `{a: {b: \"c\"}}` |\n| Parse array | `- a\\n- b` | `[\"a\", \"b\"]` |\n| Parse inline array | `[1, 2, 3]` | `[1, 2, 3]` |\n| Parse inline object | `{a: 1, b: 2}` | `{a: 1, b: 2}` |\n| Parse number | `count: 42` | `{count: 42}` |\n| Parse float | `pi: 3.14` | `{pi: 3.14}` |\n| Parse boolean true | `flag: true` | `{flag: true}` |\n| Parse boolean false | `flag: false` | `{flag: false}` |\n| Parse null | `value: null` | `{value: null}` |\n| Parse quoted string | `name: \"hello\"` | `{name: \"hello\"}` |\n| Parse multiline literal | `text: \\|\\n  line1\\n  line2` | `{text: \"line1\\nline2\"}` |\n| Parse comments | `# comment\\nkey: value` | `{key: \"value\"}` |\n| Error: invalid indentation | `a:\\nb: c` (inconsistent) | YamlParseError |\n| Error: missing colon | `key value` | YamlParseError |\n| Error: unclosed quote | `key: \"value` | YamlParseError |\n| Error: unclosed bracket | `[1, 2` | YamlParseError |\n\n**File**: `src/validate.test.ts`\n\n| Test Case | Setup | Expected |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Valid YAML file | Create temp file with valid YAML | Exit 0, success message |\n| Invalid YAML file | Create temp file with invalid YAML | Exit 1, error message |\n| File not found | Non-existent path | Exit 1, \"file not found\" message |\n| No arguments | Run without file path | Exit 1, usage message |\n\n### 7.3 Test Coverage Targets\n\n| Module | Line Coverage Target |\n|--------|---------------------|\n| yaml-parser.ts | 90% |\n| validate.ts | 85% |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### 8.1 Package.json Changes\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate\": \"bun run src/validate.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 8.2 Usage\n\n```bash\n# Validate a YAML file\nbun run validate config.yaml\n\n# Or directly\nbun src/validate.ts config.yaml\n```\n\n### 8.3 CI/CD Integration\n\n```yaml\n# Example GitHub Actions usage\n- name: Validate config\n  run: bun run validate config.yaml\n```\n\nThe validator returns exit code 1 on failure, causing CI pipelines to fail appropriately.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| add | README.md | Usage | N/A | Document new validate command |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing approach | Custom full parser | No Bun built-in; dependencies prohibited by REQ-008 | Minimal syntax checker (less thorough), external library (violates REQ-008) |\n| D2 | Parser architecture | Lexer + recursive descent | Clean separation, maintainable, handles indentation well | Single-pass parser (harder to maintain), regex-based (fragile) |\n| D3 | File location | `src/validate.ts`, `src/yaml-parser.ts` | Follows existing project structure | Separate `cli/` directory (no precedent) |\n| D4 | Test framework | bun:test | Existing project pattern | Jest (would add dependency) |\n| D5 | Error reporting | Line and column numbers | Helps developers locate issues | Message only (less helpful) |\n| D6 | Multiline string support | Include literal and folded | Common in config files | Exclude (reduced compatibility) |\n| D7 | Inline collections | Support `[]` and `{}` | Common in config files | Block-only (reduced compatibility) |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: YAML Subset Specification\n\nThis parser implements a subset of YAML 1.2 sufficient for typical configuration files.\n\n### Supported Features\n\n- **Documents**: Single document per file (no `---` document separators)\n- **Scalars**: Strings, integers, floats, booleans (`true`/`false`/`yes`/`no`), null (`null`/`~`/empty)\n- **Collections**: Block sequences, block mappings, flow sequences `[]`, flow mappings `{}`\n- **Strings**: Plain, single-quoted, double-quoted, literal block `|`, folded block `>`\n- **Comments**: Line comments starting with `#`\n- **Indentation**: Space-based (tabs rejected)\n\n### Unsupported Features (per requirements scope)\n\n- Multiple documents\n- Anchors and aliases (`&`, `*`)\n- Tags (`!`)\n- Directives (`%`)\n- Complex keys\n- Merge keys (`<<`)\n\n### Grammar (Simplified)\n\n```\ndocument    := value\nvalue       := scalar | sequence | mapping\nscalar      := string | number | boolean | null\nsequence    := block_seq | flow_seq\nmapping     := block_map | flow_map\nblock_seq   := (INDENT DASH value NEWLINE)+\nblock_map   := (INDENT KEY COLON value NEWLINE)+\nflow_seq    := LBRACKET (value (COMMA value)*)? RBRACKET\nflow_map    := LBRACE (KEY COLON value (COMMA KEY COLON value)*)? RBRACE\n```\n"
      },
      "source": "assistant"
