s (integers and floats), booleans (true/false/yes/no), null (null/~/empty)\n    - [ ] Parser supports multiline strings with literal (`|`) and folded (`>`) block scalars\n    - [ ] Parser ignores comments starting with `#`\n    - [ ] `parseYaml(content: string): unknown` function is exported as public API\n    - [ ] `YamlParseError` class is exported with `line` and `column` properties\n    - [ ] Error messages include line and column information\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Add validate script to package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#81-packagejson-changes](design.md#81-packagejson-changes)\n\n    **Effort**: 15 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `package.json` contains script entry: `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate.ts\"`\n    - [ ] Command `bun run validate <file.yaml>` invokes the validator\n\n### CLI Integration (Parallel Group 2)\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement CLI entry point in `src/validate.ts` with argument handling, file reading, and output formatting `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-cli-entry-point](design.md#32-cli-entry-point)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] CLI accepts file path as `process.argv[2]`\n    - [ ] Missing file path displays usage instructions: `Usage: bun run validate <file.yaml>` and `Validates YAML file syntax.`\n    - [ ] File reading uses `Bun.file()` API\n    - [ ] Non-existent file produces error: `Error: File not found: {filepath}`\n    - [ ] File read errors produce: `Error: Cannot read file: {filepath}` with error details\n    - [ ] Valid YAML outputs: `Valid YAML: {filepath}` and exits with code 0\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML outputs: `Invalid YAML: {filepath}` followed by `Error: {message}` and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] All error conditions (invalid YAML, file not found, read error, missing args) exit with code 1\n\n### Testing (Parallel Group 3)\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Create unit tests in `src/yaml-parser.test.ts` and `src/validate.test