        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 5 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 days\n**Started**: 2026-02-03\n\n## Overview\n\nA command-line YAML validator for the rp1-eval-project that accepts a file path, parses YAML content using a custom parser (no external dependencies), and reports validity with appropriate exit codes. The implementation consists of a custom YAML parser module, CLI entry point, package script configuration, and comprehensive unit tests.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T3] - Parser module and package.json script have no code dependencies\n2. [T2] - CLI entry point requires parser module\n3. [T4] - Tests require both parser and CLI modules\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (interface dependency: CLI imports parseYaml from parser)\n- T4 -> [T1, T2] (test dependency: tests import modules under test)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation (Parallel Group 1)\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement YAML parser with lexer and recursive descent parser in `src/yaml-parser.ts` `[complexity:complex]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-yaml-parser-module](design.md#31-yaml-parser-module)\n\n    **Effort**: 12 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Lexer tokenizes YAML content into token stream with types: KEY, VALUE, INDENT, DEDENT, NEWLINE, DASH, COLON, LBRACKET, RBRACKET, LBRACE, RBRACE, COMMA, PIPE, GREATER, EOF\n    - [ ] Lexer tracks line and column numbers for error reporting\n    - [ ] Lexer handles indentation via stack, emitting INDENT/DEDENT tokens\n    - [ ] Parser implements recursive descent for document, value, scalar, sequence, and mapping productions\n    - [ ] Parser handles key-value pairs, nested objects (indentation-based), block arrays, inline arrays `[]`, inline objects `{}`\n    - [ ] Parser correctly interprets scalars: plain strings, quoted strings (single/double), numbers (int/float/negative), booleans (true/false/yes/no), null (null/~/empty)\n    - [ ] Parser supports multiline strings with literal `|` and folded `>` block scalars\n    - [ ] Comments starting with `#` are ignored during parsing\n    - [ ] Tabs in indentation are rejected with clear error message\n    - [ ] `YamlParseError` class exported with `line` and `column` properties\n    - [ ] Public API exports `parseYaml(content: string): unknown` function\n    - [ ] Error messages include line and column information\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Add validate script to package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#81-packagejson-changes](design.md#81-packagejson-changes)\n\n    **Effort**: 15 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `package.json` contains script entry `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate.ts\"`\n    - [ ] Running `bun run validate <file.yaml>` invokes the CLI entry point\n    - [ ] No new dependencies added to package.json\n\n### CLI Integration (Parallel Group 2)\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement CLI entry point in `src/validate.ts` with argument handling, file reading, and output formatting `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-cli-entry-point](design.md#32-cli-entry-point)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] CLI accepts file path as command-line argument via `process.argv[2]`\n    - [ ] Missing file path argument displays usage: `Usage: bun run validate <file.yaml>` followed by `Validates YAML file syntax.`\n    - [ ] Missing file path argument exits with code 1\n    - [ ] File reading uses `Bun.file()` API\n    - [ ] Non-existent file displays `Error: File not found: {filepath}` and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] File read errors display `Error: Cannot read file: {filepath}` with error details and exit code 1\n    - [ ] Valid YAML displays `Valid YAML: {filepath}` and exits with code 0\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML displays `Invalid YAML: {filepath}` followed by `Error: {message}` and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] CLI imports and uses `parseYaml` from `yaml-parser.ts`\n\n### Testing (Parallel Group 3)\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Create unit tests in `src/yaml-parser.test.ts` and `src/validate.test.ts` `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests parsing empty document returns `null`\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests simple key-value pairs\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests nested objects via indentation\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests block arrays with `-` syntax\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests inline arrays `[a, b, c]`\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests inline objects `{a: 1, b: 2}`\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests number parsing (integers and floats)\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests boolean parsing (true, false)\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests null parsing\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests quoted strings (single and double)\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests multiline literal strings with `|`\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` tests comments are ignored\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.test.ts` error tests: invalid indentation, missing colon, unclosed quote, unclosed bracket all throw YamlParseError\n    - [ ] `validate.test.ts` tests valid YAML file returns exit 0 with success message\n    - [ ] `validate.test.ts` tests invalid YAML file returns exit 1 with error message\n    - [ ] `validate.test.ts` tests non-existent file returns exit 1 with \"file not found\" message\n    - [ ] `validate.test.ts` tests no arguments returns exit 1 with usage message\n    - [ ] Tests use `bun:test` framework following existing project patterns\n    - [ ] `yaml-parser.ts` achieves 90% line coverage target\n    - [ ] `validate.ts` achieves 85% line coverage target\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Create documentation for README.md - Usage `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: add\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Usage\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New Usage section created in README.md documenting the validate command\n    - [ ] Documentation includes command syntax: `bun run validate <file.yaml>`\n    - [ ] Documentation explains success and failure output messages\n    - [ ] Documentation explains exit codes (0 for valid, 1 for invalid/error)\n    - [ ] Example usage commands included\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\nFrom requirements.md:\n\n- [ ] **REQ-001**: Command can be invoked with a file path argument (e.g., `bun run validate config.yaml`)\n- [ ] **REQ-001**: Relative and absolute file paths are supported\n- [ ] **REQ-001**: Missing file path argument displays usage instructions\n- [ ] **REQ-002**: Non-existent file path produces a clear \"file not found\" error message\n- [ ] **REQ-002**: Exit code 1 is returned for non-existent files\n- [ ] **REQ-003**: Valid YAML files are correctly identified as valid\n- [ ] **REQ-003**: Invalid YAML syntax is correctly identified as invalid\n- [ ] **REQ-003**: Common YAML constructs are supported (key-value pairs, nested objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, null)\n- [ ] **REQ-004**: Success message clearly indicates the file is valid\n- [ ] **REQ-004**: Success message includes the validated file name/path\n- [ ] **REQ-005**: Error message clearly indicates the file is invalid\n- [ ] **REQ-005**: Error message includes relevant details about the parsing failure\n- [ ] **REQ-005**: Error message includes the file name/path that failed\n- [ ] **REQ-006**: Process exits with code 0 after successful validation\n- [ ] **REQ-007**: Process exits with code 1 for invalid YAML syntax\n- [ ] **REQ-007**: Process exits with code 1 for file not found\n- [ ] **REQ-007**: Process exits with code 1 for file read errors\n- [ ] **REQ-008**: No new packages added to dependencies or devDependencies\n- [ ] **REQ-008**: Implementation uses only Bun built-in capabilities or custom code\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Docs updated\n"
