        "old_string": "## Scripts\n\n- `bun run dev` - Run the main entry point\n- `bun test` - Run tests\n- `bun run lint` - Run linter\n- `bun run format` - Run formatter",
        "new_string": "## Usage\n\n### YAML Validator\n\nValidate YAML file syntax from the command line:\n\n```bash\nbun run validate <file.yaml>\n```\n\nOr run directly:\n\n```bash\nbun src/validate.ts <file.yaml>\n```\n\n#### Output Messages\n\n| Scenario | Output |\n|----------|--------|\n| Valid YAML | `Valid YAML: <filepath>` |\n| Invalid YAML | `Invalid YAML: <filepath>` followed by `Error: <message>` |\n| File not found | `Error: File not found: <filepath>` |\n| No arguments | Usage instructions |\n\n#### Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| 0 | File contains valid YAML syntax |\n| 1 | Error (invalid YAML, file not found, or missing arguments) |\n\n#### Examples\n\n```bash\n# Validate a configuration file\nbun run validate config.yaml\n\n# Validate with absolute path\nbun run validate /path/to/config.yaml\n\n# Use in CI/CD pipeline (exit code indicates success/failure)\nbun run validate config.yaml && echo \"Config is valid\"\n```\n\n## Scripts\n\n- `bun run dev` - Run the main entry point\n- `bun test` - Run tests\n- `bun run lint` - Run linter\n- `bun run format` - Run formatter\n- `bun run validate <file.yaml>` - Validate YAML file syntax"
      },
      "source": "assistant"
    },
