    {
      "id": "toolu_019eBXhBLQnQy3dTpU4nEgLd",
      "name": "Write",
      "input": {
        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/17773350/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator/src/commands/yaml-validate/README.md",
        "content": "# yaml-validate\n\nA command-line YAML syntax validator for the rp1-eval-project.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe `yaml-validate` command validates YAML files for syntax correctness without adding any external dependencies. It supports single file validation, batch validation of multiple files, and reading from stdin.\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\nbun run yaml-validate [OPTIONS] [FILES...]\ncat file.yaml | bun run yaml-validate --stdin\n```\n\n## Options\n\n| Flag | Alias | Description |\n|------|-------|-------------|\n| `--help` | `-h` | Display help message and exit |\n| `--version` | `-v` | Display version information and exit |\n| `--stdin` | `-` | Read YAML content from stdin |\n\n## Examples\n\n### Single File Validation\n\n```bash\nbun run yaml-validate config.yaml\n```\n\nOutput on success:\n```\nconfig.yaml: OK\n```\n\nOutput on failure:\n```\nconfig.yaml: FAILED\n  Line 5: Expected ':' after key\n    >   invalid key here\n```\n\n### Multiple File Validation\n\n```bash\nbun run yaml-validate config.yaml settings.yaml data.yaml\n```\n\nOutput:\n```\nconfig.yaml: OK\nsettings.yaml: FAILED\n  Line 3, Column 5: Unexpected character\n    >     bad: : value\n             ^\ndata.yaml: OK\n\nValidated 3 files: 2 passed, 1 failed\n```\n\n### Stdin Validation\n\n```bash\ncat config.yaml | bun run yaml-validate --stdin\n```\n\nOr using the `-` alias:\n```bash\necho \"key: value\" | bun run yaml-validate -\n```\n\n### Glob Patterns (via shell expansion)\n\n```bash\nbun run yaml-validate configs/*.yaml\n```\n\n### CI/CD Pipeline Integration\n\n```bash\n# Validate all YAML files in a directory\nbun run yaml-validate configs/*.yaml || exit 1\n```\n\n## Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `0` | All files validated successfully |\n| `1` | One or more validation failures |\n| `2` | Usage or argument error (e.g., no files specified) |\n\nUse these exit codes to integrate with CI/CD pipelines:\n\n```yaml\n# Example GitHub Actions step\n- name: Validate YAML configs\n  run: bun run yaml-validate configs/*.yaml\n```\n\n## Error Message Format\n\nError messages follow a consistent format:\n\n```\n<filename>: FAILED\n  Line <N>[, Column <M>]: <error description>\n    > <source line with error>\n        ^\n```\n\nComponents:\n- **Filename**: The path to the file being validated (or \"stdin\" for stdin input)\n- **Line number**: The line where the error was detected\n- **Column number**: The column position (when available)\n- **Error description**: A human-readable description of the syntax problem\n- **Source snippet**: The offending line with a caret (`^`) pointing to the error position\n\n## Validation Scope\n\nThe validator checks for YAML syntax errors including:\n\n- Improper indentation (spaces only, consistent levels)\n- Missing or misplaced colons in key-value pairs\n- Unclosed quotes (single or double)\n- Invalid list item syntax\n- Malformed multi-line strings (`|`, `>` blocks)\n- Invalid document markers (`---`, `...`)\n\n### Not Validated\n\nThe following are intentionally out of scope:\n\n- Schema validation (validating against a schema definition)\n- YAML linting (style enforcement)\n- Anchor/alias resolution\n- Custom tag validation\n- Semantic validation\n\n## File Handling\n\n### Supported Input\n\n- UTF-8 encoded text files with `.yaml` or `.yml` extension (or any text file)\n- Empty files (considered valid YAML)\n- Files containing only comments (considered valid YAML)\n- Multi-document YAML files (all documents are validated)\n\n### Rejected Input\n\n- Binary files (detected automatically and rejected with a clear error)\n- Non-existent files (reported as file not found)\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nsrc/commands/yaml-validate/\n  cli.ts           # Entry point, orchestrates validation workflow\n  args.ts          # Argument parsing and help text\n  validator.ts     # Core validation orchestration\n  formatter.ts     # Error message formatting\n  yaml-parser.ts   # YAML syntax parsing (uses Bun.YAML.parse)\n  types.ts         # TypeScript interfaces\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\nbun test src/commands/yaml-validate/\n```\n\n### Test Files\n\n- `args.test.ts` - Argument parsing tests\n- `yaml-parser.test.ts` - YAML parsing tests\n- `formatter.test.ts` - Output formatting tests\n- `validator.test.ts` - Integration tests\n"
      },
