        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/17773350/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator/design.md",
        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Created**: 2026-02-03\n**Status**: Draft\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nA command-line YAML syntax validator that integrates with the existing Bun-based project structure. The validator provides single-file and batch validation, stdin support, and clear error reporting with line numbers - all without adding new dependencies.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph Input\n        A[CLI Args] --> D[Argument Parser]\n        B[File System] --> E[File Reader]\n        C[Stdin] --> F[Stdin Reader]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core\n        D --> G[Validator Core]\n        E --> G\n        F --> G\n        G --> H[YAML Parser]\n        H --> I[Error Formatter]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Output\n        I --> J[Stdout - Success]\n        I --> K[Stderr - Errors]\n        G --> L[Exit Codes]\n    end\n```\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### Component Architecture\n\nThe validator follows a modular architecture with clear separation of concerns, matching the existing project's simple module structure.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"src/commands/yaml-validate/\"\n        CLI[cli.ts<br/>Entry Point]\n        ARG[args.ts<br/>Argument Parser]\n        VAL[validator.ts<br/>Validation Logic]\n        FMT[formatter.ts<br/>Error Formatter]\n        YAML[yaml-parser.ts<br/>YAML Syntax Parser]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"src/\"\n        IDX[index.ts<br/>Main Entry]\n    end\n\n    CLI --> ARG\n    CLI --> VAL\n    VAL --> YAML\n    VAL --> FMT\n    IDX -.->|optional integration| CLI\n```\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  commands/\n    yaml-validate/\n      cli.ts           # CLI entry point\n      args.ts          # Argument parsing\n      validator.ts     # Core validation orchestration\n      formatter.ts     # Error message formatting\n      yaml-parser.ts   # Pure YAML syntax parser\n      types.ts         # TypeScript interfaces\n      index.ts         # Module exports\n      validator.test.ts # Unit tests\n      yaml-parser.test.ts # Parser tests\n```\n\n### Component Responsibilities\n\n| Component | Responsibility |\n|-----------|----------------|\n| `cli.ts` | Entry point, orchestrates validation workflow, handles exit codes |\n| `args.ts` | Parse CLI arguments, validate inputs, detect stdin mode |\n| `validator.ts` | Coordinate file reading, parsing, and result aggregation |\n| `formatter.ts` | Format validation results for human-readable output |\n| `yaml-parser.ts` | Pure JS YAML syntax validation (no schema validation) |\n| `types.ts` | Shared TypeScript interfaces and types |\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 CLI Argument Parser (`args.ts`)\n\n```typescript\ninterface ParsedArgs {\n  files: string[];\n  help: boolean;\n  stdin: boolean;\n  version: boolean;\n}\n\n// Parsing logic:\n// - No flags + no stdin -> show usage hint\n// - --help or -h -> show help\n// - --version or -v -> show version\n// - --stdin or - -> read from stdin\n// - Remaining args -> file paths\n```\n\n### 3.2 Validator Core (`validator.ts`)\n\n```typescript\ninterface ValidationResult {\n  source: string;  // filename or \"stdin\"\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: YamlError[];\n}\n\ninterface YamlError {\n  line: number;\n  column?: number;\n  message: string;\n  snippet?: string;\n}\n\n// Main validation flow:\n// 1. Determine input sources (files, stdin)\n// 2. Read content from each source\n// 3. Parse YAML and collect errors\n// 4. Aggregate results\n// 5. Return overall success/failure\n```\n\n### 3.3 YAML Parser (`yaml-parser.ts`)\n\nThe YAML parser implements syntax validation without external dependencies. It validates:\n\n- Proper indentation (spaces only, consistent levels)\n- Key-value pair syntax\n- List item syntax\n- Multi-line string syntax (|, >)\n- Quote matching\n- Comment handling\n- Multi-document separators (---, ...)\n- Basic type detection (strings, numbers, booleans, null)\n\n**Parser Strategy:**\n1. Line-by-line tokenization\n2. Indentation stack tracking\n3. Context-aware syntax validation\n4. Error collection with position info\n\n**Limitations (by design - syntax only):**\n- No schema validation\n- No anchor/alias resolution validation\n- No custom tag handling\n- No semantic validation\n\n### 3.4 Error Formatter (`formatter.ts`)\n\n```typescript\n// Success output (stdout):\n// filename.yaml: OK\n\n// Error output (stderr):\n// filename.yaml: FAILED\n//   Line 5, Column 3: Expected ':' after key\n//     >   invalid key here\n//          ^\n\n// Batch summary (stdout):\n// Validated 5 files: 3 passed, 2 failed\n```\n\n### 3.5 Data Model\n\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n    class ParsedArgs {\n        +string[] files\n        +boolean help\n        +boolean stdin\n        +boolean version\n    }\n\n    class ValidationResult {\n        +string source\n        +boolean valid\n        +YamlError[] errors\n    }\n\n    class YamlError {\n        +number line\n        +number? column\n        +string message\n        +string? snippet\n    }\n\n    class ParserContext {\n        +number line\n        +number column\n        +number indentLevel\n        +string[] indentStack\n        +boolean inMultilineString\n    }\n\n    ValidationResult --> YamlError\n```\n\n### 3.6 Sequence Diagram - Single File Validation\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as cli.ts\n    participant Args as args.ts\n    participant Val as validator.ts\n    participant File as File System\n    participant Parser as yaml-parser.ts\n    participant Fmt as formatter.ts\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate config.yaml\n    CLI->>Args: parseArgs(argv)\n    Args-->>CLI: { files: [\"config.yaml\"], ... }\n    CLI->>Val: validate(files)\n    Val->>File: readFile(\"config.yaml\")\n    File-->>Val: content\n    Val->>Parser: parseYaml(content)\n    Parser-->>Val: { valid: true, errors: [] }\n    Val-->>CLI: [{ source: \"config.yaml\", valid: true }]\n    CLI->>Fmt: formatResults(results)\n    Fmt-->>CLI: \"config.yaml: OK\"\n    CLI->>User: stdout: output, exit(0)\n```\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Rationale |\n|-------|------------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript | Existing project language, strict mode |\n| Testing | bun:test | Existing test framework |\n| YAML Parsing | Pure TypeScript | No new dependencies constraint |\n| CLI Parsing | Manual implementation | No new dependencies constraint |\n\n**No New Dependencies**: This design explicitly avoids adding any new packages to package.json. The YAML parser is implemented in pure TypeScript.\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| Task | Component | Description | Effort |\n|------|-----------|-------------|--------|\n| T1 | args.ts | CLI argument parser with flag detection | S |\n| T2 | yaml-parser.ts | Pure TS YAML syntax validator | L |\n| T3 | formatter.ts | Error and success message formatting | S |\n| T4 | validator.ts | File reading and validation orchestration | M |\n| T5 | cli.ts | Main entry point with exit code handling | S |\n| T6 | types.ts | TypeScript interfaces | S |\n| T7 | Tests | Unit tests for parser and validator | M |\n| T8 | package.json | Add validate script | S |\n\n**Effort Key**: S = Small (< 1hr), M = Medium (1-3hr), L = Large (3-8hr)\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T2, T6] - Independent modules with no shared dependencies\n2. [T3, T4] - T3 uses error types from T2; T4 uses types from T6\n3. [T5] - Integrates all components\n4. [T7, T8] - Tests require implementation; package.json can parallel tests\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T3 -> T2 (formatter needs YamlError type from parser)\n- T4 -> T6 (validator uses shared types)\n- T4 -> T2 (validator calls parser)\n- T5 -> [T1, T3, T4] (CLI integrates arg parser, formatter, validator)\n- T7 -> [T2, T4] (tests require implementation)\n\n**Critical Path**: T2 -> T4 -> T5 -> T7\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Category | Include | Rationale |\n|---------------|---------|-----------|\n| YAML syntax validation | Yes | Core business logic |\n| Error message formatting | Yes | User-facing output correctness |\n| CLI argument parsing | Yes | App-specific behavior |\n| Exit code verification | Yes | Integration/contract testing |\n| File not found handling | Yes | App-specific error handling |\n| Stdin reading | Yes | App-specific input handling |\n\n| Test Category | Exclude | Rationale |\n|---------------|---------|-----------|\n| Bun file system APIs | No | Framework/runtime behavior |\n| Console output methods | No | Runtime behavior |\n| Process.exit behavior | No | Runtime behavior |\n\n### Test Cases\n\n**yaml-parser.test.ts:**\n- Valid YAML: empty file, simple key-value, nested objects, lists\n- Invalid YAML: bad indentation, missing colons, unclosed quotes\n- Edge cases: comments only, multi-document, trailing whitespace\n\n**validator.test.ts:**\n- Single file validation success/failure\n- Multiple file validation with mixed results\n- Non-existent file handling\n- Binary file detection\n\n**Integration tests (cli.test.ts):**\n- Exit code 0 for valid files\n- Exit code 1 for invalid files\n- Exit code 2 for usage errors\n- Help flag output\n- Stdin validation\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### Script Integration\n\nAdd to `package.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate\": \"bun run src/commands/yaml-validate/cli.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Usage Examples\n\n```bash\n# Single file\nbun run validate config.yaml\n\n# Multiple files\nbun run validate config.yaml settings.yaml\n\n# From stdin\ncat config.yaml | bun run validate --stdin\n\n# Help\nbun run validate --help\n```\n\n### CI/CD Integration\n\n```yaml\n# Example GitHub Actions usage\n- name: Validate YAML configs\n  run: bun run validate configs/*.yaml\n```\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| edit | README.md | Usage | N/A | Add validate command documentation |\n| add | src/commands/yaml-validate/README.md | All | N/A | Command-specific documentation if needed |\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing approach | Pure TypeScript implementation | Zero dependency requirement | External library (rejected - adds dependency) |\n| D2 | CLI argument parsing | Manual implementation | Zero dependency requirement; simple needs | commander.js (rejected - adds dependency) |\n| D3 | Command location | src/commands/yaml-validate/ | Follows modular organization pattern | Flat in src/ (rejected - less organized) |\n| D4 | Test location | Co-located with source | Matches existing project pattern | Separate test/ directory |\n| D5 | Error output | stderr | Unix convention for error messages | stdout (rejected - not conventional) |\n| D6 | Exit codes | 0/1/2 standard | Unix convention, CI/CD friendly | Boolean 0/1 only |\n| D7 | YAML version | 1.1/1.2 common subset | Maximum compatibility | Strict 1.2 only |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix: YAML Parser Implementation Notes\n\nThe pure TypeScript YAML parser focuses on syntax validation only. Key implementation considerations:\n\n1. **Line-based parsing**: Process YAML line by line, tracking indentation context\n2. **Indentation validation**: Enforce spaces-only, consistent indentation levels\n3. **Key detection**: Identify keys by `:` separator, handle quoted keys\n4. **List handling**: Detect `-` list markers with proper indentation\n5. **Multi-line strings**: Track `|` and `>` block scalar indicators\n6. **Quote matching**: Validate matching single/double quotes\n7. **Comment handling**: Ignore `#` comments appropriately\n8. **Document markers**: Handle `---` and `...` document boundaries\n\nThis approach validates syntactic correctness without attempting semantic validation or schema enforcement.\n"
