        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 10 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2-3 days\n**Started**: 2026-02-03\n\n## Overview\n\nA command-line YAML syntax validator that integrates with the existing Bun-based project structure. The validator provides single-file and batch validation, stdin support, and clear error reporting with line numbers. Implementation leverages Bun's native YAML support (`Bun.YAML.parse()`) to satisfy the zero-dependency constraint while simplifying development.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T2, T6] - Independent modules with no shared dependencies\n2. [T3, T4] - T3 uses error types from T2; T4 uses types from T6\n3. [T5] - Integrates all components\n4. [T7, T8] - Tests require implementation; package.json can parallel tests\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T3 -> T2 (formatter needs YamlError type from parser)\n- T4 -> T6 (validator uses shared types)\n- T4 -> T2 (validator calls parser)\n- T5 -> [T1, T3, T4] (CLI integrates arg parser, formatter, validator)\n- T7 -> [T2, T4] (tests require implementation)\n\n**Critical Path**: T2 -> T4 -> T5 -> T7\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation (Parallel Group 1)\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement CLI argument parser with flag detection `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-cli-argument-parser-argsts](design.md#31-cli-argument-parser-argsts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Parse --help and -h flags to trigger help display\n    - [ ] Parse --version and -v flags to trigger version display\n    - [ ] Parse --stdin and - flags to enable stdin mode\n    - [ ] Collect remaining arguments as file paths\n    - [ ] Return ParsedArgs interface with files, help, stdin, version fields\n    - [ ] Handle no arguments case (show usage hint)\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement YAML syntax validator using Bun.YAML.parse() `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-yaml-parser-yaml-parserts](design.md#33-yaml-parser-yaml-parserts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Wrap Bun.YAML.parse() for syntax validation\n    - [ ] Catch and parse YAML syntax errors from Bun runtime\n    - [ ] Extract line number and column from error messages\n    - [ ] Return YamlError array with line, column, message, and snippet fields\n    - [ ] Handle empty files as valid YAML\n    - [ ] Handle comments-only files as valid YAML\n    - [ ] Handle multi-document YAML (---, ...) correctly\n\n- [ ] **T6**: Define TypeScript interfaces and types `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#35-data-model](design.md#35-data-model)\n\n    **Effort**: 1 hour\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Define ParsedArgs interface (files, help, stdin, version)\n    - [ ] Define ValidationResult interface (source, valid, errors)\n    - [ ] Define YamlError interface (line, column?, message, snippet?)\n    - [ ] Export all types from types.ts\n    - [ ] Types follow strict TypeScript mode requirements\n\n### Core Logic (Parallel Group 2)\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement error and success message formatter `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#34-error-formatter-formattertss](design.md#34-error-formatter-formattertss)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Format success output as \"filename.yaml: OK\"\n    - [ ] Format error output with file, line, column, and message\n    - [ ] Include code snippet with caret pointing to error position\n    - [ ] Format batch summary as \"Validated N files: X passed, Y failed\"\n    - [ ] Success messages written to stdout\n    - [ ] Error messages written to stderr\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Implement validation orchestration with file reading `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-validator-core-validatorts](design.md#32-validator-core-validatorts)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Read file content using Bun file system APIs\n    - [ ] Read stdin content when stdin mode enabled\n    - [ ] Pass content to YAML parser and collect errors\n    - [ ] Aggregate results from multiple files\n    - [ ] Handle file not found errors gracefully\n    - [ ] Detect and reject binary/non-text files\n    - [ ] Return ValidationResult array with source and validity\n\n### Integration (Group 3)\n\n- [ ] **T5**: Implement CLI entry point with exit code handling `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#architecture](design.md#architecture)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Parse arguments using args.ts\n    - [ ] Display help when --help flag present\n    - [ ] Display version when --version flag present\n    - [ ] Call validator with files or stdin content\n    - [ ] Format and output results using formatter\n    - [ ] Exit with code 0 when all files valid\n    - [ ] Exit with code 1 when any file invalid\n    - [ ] Exit with code 2 for usage/argument errors\n\n### Finalization (Parallel Group 4)\n\n- [ ] **T7**: Write unit tests for parser and validator `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test valid YAML: empty file, simple key-value, nested objects, lists\n    - [ ] Test invalid YAML: bad indentation, missing colons, unclosed quotes\n    - [ ] Test edge cases: comments only, multi-document, trailing whitespace\n    - [ ] Test single file validation success and failure\n    - [ ] Test multiple file validation with mixed results\n    - [ ] Test non-existent file handling\n    - [ ] Test exit codes: 0 for valid, 1 for invalid, 2 for usage error\n    - [ ] Test stdin validation mode\n    - [ ] All tests pass with bun test\n\n- [ ] **T8**: Add validate script to package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#8-deployment-design](design.md#8-deployment-design)\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Add \"validate\" script pointing to src/commands/yaml-validate/cli.ts\n    - [ ] Command runnable via \"bun run validate\"\n    - [ ] Verify command works with single file argument\n    - [ ] Verify command works with multiple file arguments\n    - [ ] Verify command works with --help flag\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update README.md - Usage `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Usage\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Usage section documents the validate command\n    - [ ] Examples show single file, multiple files, and stdin usage\n    - [ ] Exit codes documented for CI/CD integration\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Create command-specific documentation `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: add\n\n    **Target**: src/commands/yaml-validate/README.md\n\n    **Section**: (new file)\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New file created with command overview\n    - [ ] All CLI flags and options documented\n    - [ ] Usage examples provided\n    - [ ] Error message format explained\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\nFrom requirements.md:\n\n### FR-001: Single File Validation\n- [ ] AC1: Given a valid YAML file path, when the validator runs, then it reports success and exits with code 0\n- [ ] AC2: Given an invalid YAML file path, when the validator runs, then it reports the syntax error with line number and exits with non-zero code\n- [ ] AC3: Given a non-existent file path, when the validator runs, then it reports file not found error and exits with non-zero code\n\n### FR-002: Multiple File Validation\n- [ ] AC1: Given multiple valid YAML file paths, when the validator runs, then it reports success for each and exits with code 0\n- [ ] AC2: Given a mix of valid and invalid files, when the validator runs, then it reports status for each file and exits with non-zero code\n- [ ] AC3: Results shall indicate which files passed and which failed\n\n### FR-003: Stdin Support\n- [ ] AC1: Given YAML piped to stdin, when the validator runs with stdin flag, then it validates the piped content\n- [ ] AC2: Given invalid YAML via stdin, when the validator runs, then it reports the syntax error\n\n### FR-004: Error Reporting\n- [ ] AC1: Error messages shall include line number where error was detected\n- [ ] AC2: Error messages shall include column/position when available\n- [ ] AC3: Error messages shall include a description of the syntax problem\n- [ ] AC4: Error messages shall be written to stderr\n\n### FR-005: Exit Codes\n- [ ] AC1: Exit code 0 indicates all files validated successfully\n- [ ] AC2: Exit code 1 indicates one or more validation failures\n- [ ] AC3: Exit code 2 indicates usage/argument errors\n\n### FR-006: Help/Usage Information\n- [ ] AC1: Running with --help or -h flag displays usage information\n- [ ] AC2: Usage information includes available options and examples\n- [ ] AC3: Running with no arguments and no stdin displays usage hint\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Tests pass (bun test)\n- [ ] Docs updated (README.md, command README)\n- [ ] No new dependencies added to package.json\n"
